# credentials never enter this repo (PI standing rule, 2026-08-26)
id_*
*ed25519*
*_rsa
*_ecdsa
authorized_keys*
known_hosts*
*.pem
*.ppk
.ssh/

# Pulled replicate workspaces (collection, 2026-08-29). 3.6 GB of raw run archive.
# Deliberately not tracked: seal_notes S7 already rules that a database-scale artefact is a
# decision to surface, not something to settle by `git add`. Hash-pinned instead by
# reps/smoke/PULLED_MANIFEST.sha256. The COLLECTED record under reps/smoke/collected/ IS tracked.
reps/smoke/s01/
reps/smoke/s02/
reps/main/*/
# ...but the COLLECTION is the terminal record, not a pulled workspace. reps/smoke/collected/ is
# tracked (29 files) and the main phase's is the same kind of artifact: the sixteen sealed records
# plus their attestation. The rule above exists to keep 30 GB of pulled workspaces out; it caught
# the 14 MB collection as collateral. Un-ignored 2026-09-02 when the collection was first made.
!reps/main/collected/
!reps/main/collected/**

# Archive tarballs are DATA, not record: 1.19 GB of binaries that GitHub hard-rejects at 100 MB
# per file. Committing them made the branch permanently unpushable and would have stranded the
# day's record on this machine -- the same failure as the 403 outage, self-inflicted. The .sha256
# attestations and ARCHIVE_NOTE.md ARE tracked, so the record states what is held and how to
# verify it; the payload lives beside the repo.
archive/**/*.tar.gz

# 25,598 pre-generated RASPA decks: derived artifacts, reproducible from
# harness/screen_gen_decks.py + screen/screen_meta_12499.json. The hash manifest IS tracked, so
# the decks the screen submits are attested without carrying 25k files in the record.
screen/decks/
